          "showLineNumbers": false,
          "showMiniMap": false
        },
        "content": "# Multiple frames sharing one refId\n\nA Grafana **refId identifies the query, not a frame**. One query can return several frames that share a refId but hold different measurements (a Prometheus query with several label sets, or a datasource that splits series by timestamp).\n\nThe single query below returns **three frames, all `refId: A`**, under label sets `line=A`, `line=B`, `line=C`, centred near **12**, **50** and **95**. A `sample` index column drives the numeric X-axis so every frame is plotted. Spec limits are LSL = 0, USL = 120.\n\n**What to verify:** the statistics table shows **three distinct rows**, each with its own n, Mean, Std Dev, Min, Max and Cp/Cpk/Pp/Ppk matching its own frame (Min/Max around 10-14, 48-53, 85-110 respectively).\n\n**Before the fix** the raw-statistics and spec-limit lookups matched frames by refId and took the first match, so all three rows displayed **frame 0's** numbers (Min 10 / Max 14 everywhere). **After the fix** frames are matched by position, so each row reflects its own frame.",
        "mode": "markdown"
      },
      "pluginVersion": "2.3.0",
      "title": "",
      "transparent": true,
      "type": "text"
    },
